      "text": [
        " اللَّهِ تَبَارَكَ وَ تَعَالَى وَ ثِيابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ قَالَ فَشَمِّرْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Abdullah Bin Sinan, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the Words of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Blessed and High, and <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:74#h4\"><a href=\"/books/quran:74#h4\">[74:4]</a></a> And your garments do purify</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Roll-up (i.e. keep them clean, not let them drag on the ground)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from ‘ Abd Allah ibn Sinan who has said the following: “About the meaning of the words of Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, . . and cleanse your clothes’, <a href=\"/#/books/quran:74#h4\"><a href=\"/books/quran:74#h4\">[74:4]</a></a> abu £ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘It means lift up (cut short) your clothes (instead of dragging them on the ground).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
